<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- widget_surface is tinted glass (1.9.116): the wallpaper's secondary
     colour (accent2_800 in dark mode at 88%, accent2_50 in light at 92%), no
     sheen. Smoked neutral at 60% and 75% came first; the owner asked for
     "more opaque with wallpaper colors". This file is the fixed-palette
     card; the Material You one is color-v31/widget_surface_dynamic.xml.

     Not frosted, and it cannot be. A RemoteViews widget has no way to blur
     what is behind it; only the launcher can, and Nothing Launcher does so
     only for its own card widgets (FrostedCardWidgetHostView). Its blurred
     wallpaper comes from com.nothing.wallpaper's AtmosphereProvider, guarded
     by a signature|privileged permission no store app can hold, and Android
     does not let an app read the wallpaper to blur it itself (both checked
     on the A024, 2026-11-03).

     History, so this is not retried: 90% (to 1.9.113) read as a flat card;
     72%/62% "frosted" (1.9.114) was plain see-through; 86%/82% with a white
     sheen (1.9.115) read as milky white. The owner wanted it like Nothing's
     own tiles: dark and see-through.

     No stroke: most system/launcher widgets don't outline their own card.
     @color/widget_border is still used for the internal dividers. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/widget_surface" />
    <corners android:radius="20dp" />
</shape>
